Origin: DHI, written for the dhi/pkg-directus package
Upstream: https://github.com/directus/directus/blob/v12.3.1/packages/utils/node/process-id.ts
Description: processId() hashes hostname, pid and time with MD5 and runs on every start
 through the extension manager (api/src/extensions/manager.ts). MD5 is rejected by the
 OpenSSL FIPS provider (ERR_OSSL_EVP_UNSUPPORTED), so directus start exits under FIPS.
 The id is ephemeral and only compared for equality on the extension reload channel,
 so the digest algorithm has no observable effect. SHA-256 is FIPS approved. The unit
 test that asserted the md5 argument follows.
Forwarded: not-yet
Applies-to: directus v12.3.1

--- a/packages/utils/node/process-id.ts
+++ b/packages/utils/node/process-id.ts
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 	if (_cache.id) return _cache.id;
 
 	const parts = [hostname(), process.pid, new Date().getTime()];
-	const hash = createHash('md5').update(parts.join(''));
+	const hash = createHash('sha256').update(parts.join(''));
 
 	_cache.id = hash.digest('hex');
 
--- a/packages/utils/node/process-id.test.ts
+++ b/packages/utils/node/process-id.test.ts
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@
 
 	processId();
 
-	expect(createHash).toHaveBeenCalledWith('md5');
+	expect(createHash).toHaveBeenCalledWith('sha256');
 	expect(hostname).toHaveBeenCalled();
